markdown <<MARKDOWN
<h1>Section 7: Bringing It Together</h1>

<div style="display: inline-block; background-color: #E4E2F8; color: #1F1976; font-weight: bold; font-size: 13px; padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 10px; margin-bottom: 12px;">Aligns to curriculum Lesson 13</div>

<p>This section prepares you to teach one curriculum lesson, but it's a three-day project, not a single-day lesson. There's no new content here. Students apply everything from this unit, decision trees, conditionals, functions, debugging, to build their own conversational AI project from scratch.</p>

<div style="background-color: #F7F7FB; border-left: 4px solid #4C42CF; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px 16px; margin-bottom: 16px;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5;"><b>Curriculum Lesson 13:</b> Conversational AI Project</div>
  <a href="PASTE_AIF_Y2_UNIT_1_LESSON_13_URL_HERE" style="display: inline-block; background-color: #4C42CF; color: #FFFFFF; font-weight: bold; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 13px;">View Curriculum Lesson 13</a>
</div>

<hr>

<p><b>In this section, you'll:</b></p>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Walk through the full project pipeline: topic choice, decision tree, Python implementation, written reflection</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Review the rubric, so you know what you're actually grading before students start</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Build a mini example yourself, end to end, before watching students do the same</div>
<div style="margin-bottom: 6px; font-size: 16px;">&bull; Get pacing notes for all three project days</div>
<div style="font-size: 16px;">&bull; Get ahead of the most common failure mode: a program that runs, but whose decision tree doesn't actually branch in any meaningful way</div>

<div style="background-color: #E4E2F8; border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 16px 0;">
  <div style="font-size: 16px; color: #222222; line-height: 1.5;"><b>&#128161; Notice as you explore:</b> this project introduces one genuinely new piece of syntax, an <code>ask()</code> function, nowhere else in the unit. Worth knowing that going in, since students will hit it with no prior setup.</div>
</div>

<hr>

<div style="display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-top: 24px; max-width: 700px;">
